hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20588","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: I heard Mutarrif narrating from a bedouin, he said: I saw on the foot of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a patched sandal."
"20863","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal narrating from Mutarrif, from a Bedouin, that he saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) patched sandals."
"21017","Ismail narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: I was with Mutarrif in the camel market, and a Bedouin came with a piece of hide or a sack, and he said: who recites, or is there among you one who recites? I said: yes, so I took it, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh, a clan of Ukl: they, if they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and separate from the polytheists, and acknowledge the fifth in their spoils and the share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his select portion, then they are safe by the security of Allah and His Messenger. Then one of the people said to him: did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that you can narrate to us? He said: yes. They said: then narrate to us, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard him say: whoever is pleased that much of the rancor of his chest goes away, let him fast the month of patience, or three days of every month. Then the people, or some of them, said to him: did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: do you think I am accused of lying against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And Ismail said once: do you fear? By Allah, I will not narrate to you a hadith for the rest of the day. Then he went away."
"21018","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Harun ibn Riab, from Ibn al-Shikhkhir, from a man of Banu Uqaysh, he said: with him is the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: fasting three days of the month removes the rancor of the chest."
"21019","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah and Abu al-Dahma, they said: they used to travel often toward this House, they said: we came upon a man of the desert people, and the Bedouin said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and began teaching me from what Allah, blessed and exalted is He, taught him, and he said: you will not leave anything out of fear of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, except that Allah will give you better than it."
"21020","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, he said: we were sitting at al-Mirbad, and a man of the desert people came upon us, when we saw him we said: this is as if a man who is not of the townspeople. He said: yes, and with him was a letter in a piece of hide, he said, and perhaps he said in a piece of sack, and he said: this is a letter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, this is a letter from Muhammad the Prophet, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh, and they are a clan of Ukl: you, if you establish prayer and give zakat and separate from the polytheists and give the fifth of the spoils, then the share of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the select portion, and perhaps he said: and his select portion, then you are safe by the security of Allah, blessed and exalted is He, and the security of His Messenger. Then he mentioned, meaning the hadith of al-Jurayri."
"21021","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawadah al-Qushayri narrated to me, he said: a man of the desert people narrated to me, from his father, and his father had been a captive with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: no prayer is accepted in which the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah) is not recited."
"21026","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Abu Qatadah and Abu al-Dahma narrated to us, Affan said: and they used to perform Hajj often, they said: we came upon a man of the desert people, and the Bedouin said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and began teaching me from what Allah taught him. Among what I memorized from him was that he said: you will not leave anything out of fear of Allah, blessed and exalted is He, except that Allah will give you better than it."
